    % Experience
    \section*{Experience}

    \subsection*{\href{http://www.datacrt.com}{DataCRT}} \hfill Oakland, CA \\
    \textbf{Principal Engineer} \hfill Feb 2025 -- Present

    Leads DataCRT's energy practice, helping clients design robust data ingestion and analysis products for their energy and environmental data. Also the PM and lead developer of the firm's internal techno-economic-analysis (TEA) optimization library.
    \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
        \item PM and lead developer of the in-house TEA library for DER, grid-battery, and microgrid systems, providing optimal sizing and dispatch plus full project economics (NPV, IRR, payback, LCOE, emissions).
        \begin{itemize}
            \item Designed a swappable sizing and dispatch optimizer interface with two interchangeable backends --- NREL's REopt.jl (Julia) or custom-defined CVXPY linear programs --- united behind a single contract for maximum reliability vs.\ modeling flexibility depending on client needs.
            \item Built CVXPY-based microgrid and battery-storage dispatch optimization and port-terminal electrification use cases; added emissions and carbon-abatement-frontier analysis, batch scenario ranking, and tornado sensitivity analysis to support client investment decisions.
        \end{itemize}
        \item Leading energy analysis on a \$3M CEC grant proposal to improve net-load forecasting of behind-the-meter solar, battery, and EV resources for a major container port.
        \item Authored PRDs and technical scoping for a utility bill-intelligence platform (rate-plan optimization); technical architect of data-ingestion and processing systems for utility data.
    \end{itemize}

    \subsection*{\href{http://www.weavegrid.com}{WeaveGrid}} \hfill San Francisco, CA \\
    \textbf{Software Engineer / Data \& Analytics Engineer} \hfill Oct 2021 -- Dec 2024
    \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
        \item One of the initial engineers on a new greenfield product line building \href{https://www.weavegrid.com/utilities}{WeaveGrid for Utilities}, a platform for utilities to manage and optimize residential and commercial EV charging; built the data pipeline, REST/GraphQL API, and React interfaces.
        \item Built the internal data warehouse, ETL pipeline, and ML forecasting/analytics used to evaluate utility EV-charging programs across tens of thousands of connected EVs and EVSE chargers (hundreds of GWh daily), including behind-the-meter EV spatial-temporal optimization for utilities.
    \end{itemize}

    \subsection*{\href{http://pingthings.io/}{PingThings}} \hfill Remote \\
    \textbf{Product Manager} \hfill Oct 2020 -- Oct 2021
    \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
        \item Owned product for \href{https://www.pingthings.io/platform.html}{PredictiveGrid}, a cloud platform for high-frequency (1--100 GHz) grid sensor data used by several of the top-30 US utilities and grid operators. Set the product roadmap, managed the development team, and drove go-to-market strategy with the executive team.
    \end{itemize}

    \subsection*{\href{http://www.qlear.io/}{QLEAR.io}} \hfill Shanghai, China \\
    \textbf{Head of Product} \hfill Aug 2016 -- Jun 2018
    \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
        \item Head of Product for an IoT SaaS platform optimizing indoor air quality and energy use across commercial and retail buildings for Fortune 500 real-estate and retail firms, with thousands of connected devices across a portfolio of thousands of buildings. Set the product roadmap, managed the development team, and drove go-to-market strategy with the executive team.
    \end{itemize}

